+## Packaged runtime limits
+
+Repository rules and the user's authorization override these playbooks. They do not grant authority for external writes or deployment.
+
+For `tasks[]` and `chain[]`, set `readonly` on each item. Top-level `readonly` is single-mode only. Children reload global Pi resources but do not inherit parent CLI tool restrictions or `--no-mcp`. Read-only ordinary tools do not sandbox extensions or MCP.
+
+The installed package may be read-only. Before running a TypeScript helper that bootstraps dependencies, copy the entire `scripts/` directory beside this skill to a fresh writable temporary directory. Run the copied helper by absolute path from the task's working directory. Allow frozen-lockfile dependency installation only there and only when network access is permitted. Remove the copy afterward.
+
 ## Subagents
 
 Use `pstack_task` for every pstack delegation. Use `agent: "poteto-agent"` for code-writing delegates and ad-hoc helpers inside playbook steps. Routed skills such as `how`, `why`, `interrogate`, `reflect`, `swarm`, `arena`, and `architect` name their own exact roles. Do not replace those roles with a generic one.
